FAQ

What are ultra-wide bandgap semiconductors?
Ultra-wide bandgap semiconductors are advanced semiconductor materials with significantly wider energy bandgaps than conventional silicon, enabling potential advantages in high-voltage, high-temperature, and high-frequency applications.

Why are ultra-wide bandgap materials important?
They can enable semiconductor devices designed for demanding electrical and thermal environments while supporting improved power-handling and switching performance.

Where can ultra-wide bandgap semiconductors be used?
Potential applications include power electronics, energy systems, industrial equipment, high-temperature electronics, aerospace, defense, and other advanced semiconductor applications.

